/* The end-of-combat panel. It lives in the combat scene, on a PanelSettings at sortingOrder 50:
   above the HUD (10) and below the loading overlay (100), which has to be able to cover it when
   the scene transition starts. PS_CombatEnd is ScaleWithScreenSize 1920x1080 + Shrink, like the
   menus: without that the fixed 1920x1080 stage would not fit the screen.

   Unlike the pause menu, the fight is over: there is nothing left to read in the scene, so the
   screen is a full parchment (.screen-root + .parchment-stage from STL_Menu.uss) and the game is
   not visible behind it. One layout for victory and defeat, as in the mockups: only the title
   string changes, there is no per-outcome colour.

   Input blocking is not code: because the root is full-screen and pickable,
   UIPointerTracker.IsPointerOverUI catches it and WorldInteractor / GridInputHandler stop picking
   up clicks on the world.

   Coordinates and font sizes are measured on the Figma exports (1920x1080). */

.combat-end-root {
    /* display: none when hidden — NOT just opacity 0. A transparent but still drawn element would
       stay pickable and would eat clicks for the whole combat. */
    display: none;
    opacity: 0;
}

/* Centred on y ~350. Same cap height as the pause menu's title in the mockups, hence the same
   96px, not a larger size. */
.combat-end-title {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 290px;
    width: 100%;
    height: 120px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 96px;
    color: rgb(0, 0, 0);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* The box is the hover/click surface, centred on the stage and wider than the longest entry; the
   underline and the quill anchor to the text, not to this box. */
.combat-end-entry {
    position: absolute;
    left: 660px;
    width: 600px;
    height: 60px;
    font-size: 72px;
}

/* Row centres from the mockup: ~655 and ~765. */
.combat-end-entry--1 { top: 625px; }
.combat-end-entry--2 { top: 735px; }

/* left/top are only the pre-layout start: SelectionMarker.MoveTo overwrites both. */
.combat-end-marker {
    left: 660px;
    top: 625px;
    height: 60px;
}

/* Same quill as the pause menu: 112px, ~40px visible gap to the text, centred on the 60px row. */
.combat-end-marker .selection-marker__quill {
    left: -136px;
    top: -26px;
    width: 112px;
    height: 112px;
}
